{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/caps/user.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-14T03:18:07.372607Z","id":"94ab5cdaf4de5bbed63a3fac96b1c4d50f4102b26fc9a41c5430dbdc8a8c63ea","body":{"detail":"The header says Clax has no guests; a hosted instance has them, and `me()` answers isOwner and canEdit from env.token alone, so a hosted guest reads as a member and a member with publish rights as unable to edit. The server enforces the rights, so a page cannot gain anything by it, but a page that trusts these fields misbehaves.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":1},"end":{"line":10},"content_hash":"755f77437e4c357f9c227a909b248314d87a2588d394fbdfe8c65d3a5fbd33f8"},"suggested_fix":"Carry the hosted viewer's guest flag and rights in CapEnv.viewer and answer from them.","summary":"The user capability tells pages guest: false and computes isOwner and canEdit from the shell token, which is wrong on a hosted instance","tags":["hosted","web","review","session:claude-code:6847a238-376f-486d-8e40-4d0fa676e347"]}}
